From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 12:06:25 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 10/13] Round 10: Write batch JSON with pre-encoded keys

Batch::write_json writes the envelope, record and metrics keys, status
strings, schema, version and the trace column list as pre-encoded
bytes in serde's field order. Ids, details, failure metrics, numbers
and traces still go through serde_json, so strings and floats use the
same escaping and formatter. evaluate_json and scores_json use the
writer; the CLI Value path keeps the derived serializer. A unit test
requires byte equality with serde_json::to_string for complete,
failed, cancelled, work-limited, traced and lean batches and for
escaped ids, details and JSON failure metrics.

Workload: serial (96 full records, 62 steps each, one worker).
Before median: 0.1071 ms. After median: 0.0876 ms. Speedup: 1.22x.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
